content:
DrorPay includes a signature header when your platform has a secret configured:
X-DrorPay-Signature: sha256=<hmac_signature>

Verification (Node.js):
```js
const crypto = require('crypto');
function verifyWebhookSignature(payload, signature, secret) {
  const expected = crypto
    .createHmac('sha256', secret)
    .update(JSON.stringify(payload))
    .digest('hex');
  return `sha256=${expected}` === signature;
}
```

Critical: use JSON.stringify(req.body) exactly — do NOT re-parse or re-serialize the payload object. The signature is computed over the exact bytes sent. Verify the signature BEFORE processing any payload content.
